        <mxCell id="c134" value="The fitted line, February 2024 to December 2026" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=12;fontColor=#2C3E50;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="495.476" y="388" width="266.792" height="20" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c135" value="&lt;i&gt;Each point is a month, February 2024 to December 2026; the fit leaves out January 2024, which has 491 standard hours and no payroll or overhead entry to 1090 (its one payroll, of salaries, went to 5080). The overhead entries move with output at about the applied rate; the payroll does not, and the months with three pay dates (March 2024, August 2024, January 2025, August 2025, January 2026, July 2026) carry a third payroll with no more output.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#5D6D7E;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="418" width="860" height="53" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
